{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "id": "cathedral",
  "kind": "building",
  "notes": "Cathedral (12×16): a warm dressed-stone cathedral facing the road — a tall nave with clerestory windows over two aisles, buttresses with pinnacles and flying buttresses, a transept with rose windows in both gables and a slender flèche over the crossing, an apse with three radiating chapels; the west front has two square towers with belfries, parapets and slate spires with brass finials, a gabled centre with the great rose window (blue glass, pale tracery) over the deep portal. Roofs are slate (the walls stay warm stone). In front a paved forecourt with steps, a fountain, trees in stone planters, lamps and a low wall with gate piers; behind the apse a walled close with lawns, trees and gravestones.",
